(275, 1, '39', 'Black Trees', 'All the trees around the distillery have black bark. This is caused by a fungus called Baudoinia compniacensis that feeds on the ethanol vapor in the air from the distillation and aging process. Supposedly this helped the feds find moonshine stills in the woods back in the day.', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/275_1_1024.jpg', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/275_1_200c.jpg', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/275_1_600.jpg', '1024', '683', 1, 173, '2011-05-11 12:42:00'),
(276, 1, '39', 'Jack Daniels Spring', 'This is where the water comes from that is used to make Jack Daniels whiskey. Its a little cave out behind the old office.', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/276_1_1024.jpg', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/276_1_200c.jpg', 'http://50states.s3.amazonaws.com/276_1_600.jpg', '1024', '683', 1, 82, '2011-05-11 12:43:25'),
